{% comment %}
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  PHOTO ROLODEX — LavaEndpoint: setup                            ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Paste this whole file into the CodeTemplate field of a         ║
║  LavaEndpoint named "setup" (HTTP Method: GET) that belongs to   ║
║  the "rolodex" LavaApplication.                                  ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Requires Rock RMS 18.0 or later. This project targets 18.0+     ║
║  exclusively -- see DEPLOYMENT.md for why.                        ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Endpoint settings (Admin Tools > CMS > Lava Applications):      ║
║    Slug:                 setup                                  ║
║    HTTP Method:          Get                                    ║
║    Enabled Lava Commands: sql                                    ║
║    Security Mode:        Application View (or your preference)  ║
║                                                                  ║
║  This template returns ONLY the inner content that goes inside  ║
║  the host page's <div id="rolodex-app">...</div> -- it must     ║
║  NOT re-emit that wrapping div itself, since the host page swaps ║
║  this response directly into that div's innerHTML.              ║
║                                                                  ║
║  SOURCES ARE PERSON TAGS -- there is no hardcoded CONFIGURATION  ║
║  block to maintain. The dropdown below is built live from every ║
║  active, organization-wide Tag scoped to the Person entity. To   ║
║  add a new "list" to the game, an admin/staff member just tags   ║
║  the people they want (Person profile > tag icon, or a Grid's    ║
║  "Tag" bulk action) -- nothing in this file needs to change.     ║
║  Personal tags (owned by one staff member) are deliberately      ║
║  excluded so one person's private tags don't clutter everyone    ║
║  else's dropdown -- see the SQL query below.                     ║
║                                                                  ║
║  The List field uses Rock's built-in {[ dropdown ]} Lava          ║
║  shortcode (longlistenabled:'true') rather than a hand-rolled     ║
║  <select>, so it gets Rock's enhanced/searchable dropdown for     ║
║  free. Lava shortcodes are not gated by "Enabled Lava Commands"   ║
║  -- only sql/entitycommand-style commands are, so no extra        ║
║  setting is needed for this.                                     ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  ^/{applicationSlug}/{endpointSlug} is Rock's shorthand for calling a
  Lava Endpoint from hx-get/hx-post (confirmed against a real working
  Lava Application build elsewhere in this repo). Update "rolodex" if
  you use a different LavaApplication slug.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign gameUrl = '^/rolodex/game' %}

{% comment %}
  Rock.SystemGuid.EntityType.PERSON is a stable GUID across every Rock
  install (unlike EntityType.Id, which is just an auto-increment value
  that can differ instance to instance) -- confirmed against
  Rock/SystemGuid/EntityType.cs. OwnerPersonAliasId IS NULL means an
  organization-wide tag, not a personal one owned by a single staff
  member's login.
{% endcomment %}
{% sql %}
  SELECT t.Id, t.Name
  FROM Tag t
  JOIN EntityType et ON et.Id = t.EntityTypeId
  WHERE et.Guid                = '72657ED8-D16E-492E-AC12-144C5E7567E7'
    AND t.OwnerPersonAliasId   IS NULL
    AND t.IsActive              = 1
  ORDER BY t.[Order], t.Name
{% endsql %}
{% assign tags = results %}

<div class="text-center pt-4 pb-3">
  <i class="fa fa-id-card-o text-primary" style="font-size: 3rem;"></i>
  <h2 class="mt-2 mb-1">Photo Rolodex</h2>
  <p class="text-muted mb-0">Learn names by face, one person at a time.</p>
</div>

<form hx-get="{{ gameUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app">

  {% comment %}
    Rock ships a built-in {[ dropdown ]} Lava shortcode (seeded in the same
    v18 migration that added Lava Applications, guid
    7BA8EA13-BC09-4075-B0AF-F88AB1203953) rather than a hand-rolled
    <select>. With longlistenabled:'true' it renders the same
    chosen-select chosen-select-absolute classes documented in the Rock UI
    skill, plus its own inline <script> that calls jQuery's .chosen()
    immediately after the markup renders. That script re-runs every time
    this shortcode's output is generated, including on the HTMX swap that
    loads this setup screen, so it does not depend on Rock's page-load-only
    global init to pick it up. Options come from child [[ item ]] tags,
    built dynamically here from the tags query above; a leading blank item
    keeps the "-- Choose a List --" placeholder and required-field behavior
    identical to the previous plain <select>.
  {% endcomment %}
  {[ dropdown label:'List' name:'tag' longlistenabled:'true' isrequired:'true' ]}
    [[ item value:'' text:'-- Choose a List --' ]][[ enditem ]]
    {% for t in tags %}
    [[ item value:'{{ t.Id }}' text:'{{ t.Name }}' ]][[ enditem ]]
    {% endfor %}
  {[ enddropdown ]}

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Game Mode</label>
    <div class="rd-mode-group">
      <input type="radio" name="mode" id="rd-flip" value="flip" checked>
      <label for="rd-flip" class="btn btn-default">
        <i class="fa fa-eye"></i>&nbsp; Tap to Reveal
      </label>
      <input type="radio" name="mode" id="rd-quiz" value="quiz">
      <label for="rd-quiz" class="btn btn-default">
        <i class="fa fa-list-ul"></i>&nbsp; Multiple Choice
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <div class="checkbox mt-0">
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="trk" value="1" checked>
        Track score (Multiple Choice only)
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="checkbox mt-0">
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" name="minfo" value="1" checked>
        Show more about each person (household, campus, etc.) after answering
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-block">
    <i class="fa fa-play"></i>&nbsp; Start
  </button>
</form>
